James inquired about exporting references in a Zotero collection while retaining information about subfolder categorization. I explained that Zotero does not offer a direct feature for this and suggested using tags or a script with the Zotero API. He then asked how to use the API, and I guided him through creating an API key and constructing endpoint URLs. James encountered an issue where shared collections were not visible, prompting a discussion on identifying group IDs and accessing shared collections. After confirming the structure of top-level collections, he sought a script to traverse collection hierarchies. I provided a recursive script to report titles and categories. Subsequently, James raised concerns about potential API limits on collections, leading to recommendations for handling pagination in both collection and item queries to ensure comprehensive retrieval of data.
